LOCAL HEADER-OCR RECOVERY -- run log
Tool: C:\PatoLex-scratch\_header_ocr.py  (+ _scan_headers.py, _validate_*.py, _apply_1866.py)
Goal: token-efficient LOCAL recovery of "missing" chapters whose page-TOP running-head
("CHAPTER N" / "Chap. N" / roman) was skipped/garbled by full-page OCR. No agent vision
tokens; no DB writes; additive only; merged/certified files untouched.

Engine: Tesseract 5.4.0 (C:\Users\patolex\AppData\Local\Tesseract-OCR\tesseract.exe)
Python: C:\PatoLex-scratch\ocr-engines\surya-venv\Scripts\python.exe (has pytesseract, PIL, PyMuPDF, surya)

================================================================================
TOOL DESIGN
================================================================================
[2026-06-21] DESIGN | _header_ocr.py | OK
  * header_ocr_page(img): crops top strips (fracs 0.10/0.14/0.18/0.22) of the page
    image, upscales 2x, runs Tesseract --oem 1 at psm 6/7/11, parses the first
    legible chapter number. Optional Surya fallback (lazy-loaded).
  * parse_chapter_from_text(): arabic ("CHAPTER 482","CHAP. 482","[Ch. 482]") and
    roman ("CHAP. XXVI","CHAPTER CCCCLXXXII"). roman_to_int handles archaic ADDITIVE
    forms (CCCC=400, XXXX=40, VIIII=9) AND standard subtractive (XL, CD, CM).
  * OCR-tolerance (critical for early-era): the chapter word "CHAP."/"Chap." is
    routinely corrupted by Tesseract to "Cuap."/"CHap."/"Cnap."/"Cuar." -- lead-in
    regex accepts C/O + 2-3 letters + (p|r). Roman tokens normalize O->C, U->V
    (the 'CCC' triple often OCRs as 'CCO'). A leading word-boundary + required
    separator suppress false hits from prose/dates ("March 12" no longer matches).
  * Parser self-test: 12/12 cases pass (incl. all additive-roman forms).

