[2026-06-22] MULTIACT-METHOD | NEW band-free mid-page header recovery (_scan_headers_multiact.py + _apply_multiact.py) | OK
  Goal: recover the residual chapters where 2-3 short acts share one printed page and the
    page's 2nd/3rd "CHAPTER N" header sits MID-PAGE, eluding the top-favoring scanners
    (_header_ocr top-strip crop; _scan_headers full-page psm 6/4/11 block union).
  Technique: run Tesseract psm 11 (SPARSE) + psm 6 (block) over the FULL page at multiple
    render DPIs (200/240/300). Sparse mode segments isolated text regions, so a mid-page
    header set off by whitespace reads as its own line instead of dissolving into the body
    block. (An earlier 8-band slicing design worked but cost ~10s/page and MANUFACTURED
    roman misreads; the sparse full-page pass is ~3s/page, equal recall, no sibling noise.)
  PRECISION GUARD (critical, roman volumes): roman headers are DPI-FRAGILE -- the glyph count
    of a CCCC.../DCXVIII... token shifts with resolution. A confirm therefore requires the
    EXACT oracle number to read at >=2 distinct render DPIs (vote>=2); a single-DPI read is
    left residual. Verified on 1872: a multi-DPI re-audit of all 17 confirmations showed the
    printed roman token matches the oracle EXACTLY in every case (CCCCXCIII=493, DCXVIII=618,
    CCLXXXVIII=288, ...); a naive single-different-DPI (240) re-read had falsely "mismatched"
    11/17 purely from DPI fragility -- multi-DPI agreement is the correct test, vote count
    alone (within one DPI) is NOT (a real mid-page win and a sibling misread both poll once).
  Also: only TIGHT windows scanned (multi-act pages share a page with a present neighbor);
    windows wider than 12 pp are garbled/edge cases, skipped for the visual fallback.
  CONFIRM-ONLY, additive: origin=local_header_ocr_multiact, status=image_verified,
    printed_number_confirmed=true, chapter_int_final==oracle, dpi_votes recorded. No DB/
    merged/certified writes. Durable lesson: LESSON_2026-06-22_multiact_band_scan_header_ocr.md

